From: Erik Dubois <erik.dubois@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Kiro: depend on quickshell from extra, not quickshell-git

caelestia-shell v2.5.0 pins quickshell commit 2d3b3e9 (2026-08-29) in its
flake.lock, and that commit is an ancestor of the v0.3.2 tag (2026-10-08)
that Arch extra ships. So extra's quickshell carries everything v2.5.0 was
built against, and the KiroTux Quickshell editions keep one quickshell
package instead of a conflicting -git build. Recheck on every bump.

Local Kiro delta, not upstream AUR.
---
--- a/PKGBUILD	2026-11-09 09:12:56.440198953 +0100
+++ b/PKGBUILD	2026-11-09 09:12:56.440851900 +0100
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 license=('GPL-3.0-only')
 depends=(
     'caelestia-cli'
-    'quickshell-git'
+    'quickshell>=0.3.2'
     'glibc'
     'gcc-libs'
 
